@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Codename Shepherd</PageTitle>

<h1>About Codename Shepherd</h1>

<h2>What is this</h2>
<p>This is an early access application meant to streamline signups for groups.</p>

<p>It is open to sign ups. However expect bugs.</p>

<h2>What's with the name</h2>
<p>Right now it is still in early access. Hence the <code>Codename</code> part of Codename Shepherd.</p>

<p>The <code>Shepherd</code> part is meant to illustrate how it is like herding cats to organize large groups. 
That's also where the temporary logo comes from.</p>

<h2>Additional FAQs</h2>

<details>
    <summary>What are your current features?</summary>
    <ul>
        <li>Create a form to allow signups that supports start time, location, description, slots, and quantity for that slot</li>
        <li>Publish that list and allow sign ups without logging in (but providing details)</li>
        <li>Form creator can delete sign ups</li>
        <li>Form creator can view an HTML report or CSV report of signups</li>
    </ul>
</details>

<details>
    <summary>What features are you planning?</summary>
    <ul>
        <li>Allow form types of shifts (date &amp; times)</li>
        <li>Allow form types of just RSVP</li>
        <li>Email notifications</li>
    </ul>
</details>

<details>
    <summary>Info for nerds (tech stack)?</summary>
    <ul>
        <li>Database - MongoDB</li>
        <li>Web App - Blazor Server</li>
        <li>Authentication - Auth0</li>
        <li>Email - SendGrid?</li>
    </ul>
</details>

<details>
    <summary>Who are your competitors?</summary>
    <p>The main competitor in the space is SignupGenius although Doodle seems to be entering the space</p>
</details>